# Approval

CLI with no flags is a **dry-run**: live `awaiting_shipment` → counts + process names. It does **not** write Packing Input, catalogs, or Output.

`--run` writes one CSV per process into Packing Input **only** when the supervisor already said **run**, into the shift they named. `RESEND` / `UNMATCHED` land in that shift folder.

**Chat fast path (locked 2026-10-07, shift ask 2026-10-14, catalog step removed 2026-10-20):** when the supervisor says **run the group sorter** / **group my awaiting shipment** / **run the sorter** (or clear equivalent) **and names the shift**, run that shift **immediately** — no `seed_catalog_misses.py`, no packing dry-run first, no long pre-amble. The pool is current ShipStation `awaiting_shipment` only. Do not skip an order because it already appears in an earlier shift CSV. Short log summary when done. If the shift was not named in that message, **ask which shift** and do not run yet. That ask applies in every chat and every new session. Asking for a dry-run only stays dry-run.

**Add unmatched (separate, locked 2026-10-20):** only when the supervisor says **add unmatched**. Run `python "Order Grouping Sorter/scripts/seed_catalog_misses.py"`. It uses the sorter finish gate, then `Custom Label Database/scripts/add_labels.py --csv` against `Custom_Label_Database (Areeb).csv` (backup first). Peer or definite supplier only; `Customise` from `.cursor/rules/custom-label-database/fill-pipeline.mdc`; no guessing; no `--all-spc`. It does not write Packing Input and is not part of **run the group sorter**.

The sorter process still only reads catalogs. A separate full-catalog fill stays a different job (supervisor **fill / run**). 3rd shift and later write overdue, blank, and the run-day ship-by, plus tag `1004- Personalised Design-Ready-` when ship-by is later (locked 2026-10-22). A later ship-by without that tag stays out.
